From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:15:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Add a ramoops region

Reserve 1 MiB of DRAM at 0x60000000 for pstore/ramoops, so the kernel
log of a panic or an oops can be read after a warm reset.
DRAM keeps its contents across the reset paths of the board (PSCI
SYSTEM_RESET and the watchdog), the boot chain does not write the
region, and it lies in the first GiB of DRAM (DRAM starts at
0x40000000, A733 manual, 2 Memory Map), away from the SCP firmware region.

A dump record is 128 KiB, the size of the default kernel log buffer
(LOG_BUF_SHIFT 17). The region also holds a 256 KiB console record for
kernels built with CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE, so six dump records fit next
to it. ECC (16 bytes per block) keeps a record with bit errors from
being read back as a valid log.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the record of a panic is read back after
the warm reset.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 69c077594490..027cdedfab7f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -59,6 +59,15 @@ scp@48100000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x48100000 0x0 0x100000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/* pstore records, kept in DRAM across a warm reset */
+		ramoops@60000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x60000000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	/*
